   ],
   "ocr": "in 1978 [31]. The study participants were aged 50 y and older, as in this study, and were examined by indirect ophthalmoscopy as well as photography. Higher levels of ‘‘senile macular degenera- tion’’, as AMD was then termed, were reported than in this study, affecting 17.4% of participants in the study. It is likely that the"
